      "message": "Hi Alan,\n\nConcerning the vsock connection we discussed recently, it seems that I cannot close the fd after a rebase today with the following error (it worked before).\n\n```\n08-30 13:33:01.682  5733  5791 W ParcelFileDescriptor: Unable to inform peer: Cannot close socket file descriptor\n08-30 13:33:01.680  5733  5733 W Thread-4: type\u003d1400 audit(0.0:27): avc: denied { getopt } for scontext\u003du:r:untrusted_app:s0:c126,c256,c512,c768 tcontext\u003du:r:virtualizationservice:s0 tclass\u003dvsock_socket permissive\u003d0 app\u003dcom.android.microdroid.benchmark\n08-30 13:33:01.685  5733  5768 I MicrodroidBenchmarks: Log: 08-30 11:33:01.804   131   138 I microdroid_launcher: VM:Finished reading data.\n```\n\nThis code runs on the host. Is there any other way to close the socket file descriptor in the virt package?",
